Upstream-Name: driftwire
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/longtimeno-c/mediaviewer/issues
Source: https://github.com/longtimeno-c/mediaviewer
Comment: driftwire is the command line of MediaViewer's Driftwire add-on
 (src/addons/driftwire, docs/design/28-driftwire.md "From a terminal"),
 built from the release's tagged source. /usr/bin/driftwire links libsodium,
 BLAKE3 and FTXUI statically (the pinned vcpkg ports; their upstream
 sources are named in each stanza below), and the GCC C++ runtime
 (libstdc++, libgcc) under the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1. It needs
 only the C library at run time and opens libsecret and libsystemd when
 they are there. The release page that carries this package also offers
 its source.

